{"author":{"id":"2462ded6f56967dde059994c39a506c79e39e5dfd10c5a07f07a23a5652a8353"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1773842865,"nonce":"4H2Uc2YItjfUChX2HzNmMwLx/p8=","title":"nightshift accept should not block on unrelated uncommitted files","message":"Currently `check_working_tree_clean()` in `host/merge.py` exits with an error if ANY tracked file is modified, even if the changes are completely unrelated to the merge.\n\nExample: `docs/roadmap.md` is modified locally → `nightshift accept` refuses to merge an agent branch that doesn't touch `docs/roadmap.md` at all.\n\n**Fix options:**\n1. Remove the clean-tree check entirely — git merge will fail with a clear message if there are actual conflicts with uncommitted changes\n2. Only check for changes in files that overlap with the merge diff\n3. Downgrade to a warning instead of a hard block\n\nOption 1 is simplest and most correct — git already handles this case.","files":null}]}